@startuml system-workflow-simple
title Docling Studio — Workflow (simplified)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7E0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C46C

actor "User" as User
participant "Web UI" as UI #E8F5E9
participant "Converter" as Conv #FFF3E0
participant "RAG" as RAG #F3E5F5
boundary "Cohere Embed" as Cohere #ECEFF1
database "PostgreSQL\n(pgvector)" as PG #ECEFF1
boundary "Anthropic Claude" as Claude #ECEFF1

== Step 1 — Upload and convert ==
User -> UI : drops **Workshop.pptx**
UI -> Conv : convert
Conv -> Conv : Docling + OCR → **Markdown**

== Step 2 — Chunk, embed, store ==
UI -> RAG : embed the Markdown
RAG -> RAG : split into **chunks**
RAG -> Cohere : embed chunks
Cohere --> RAG : vectors
RAG -> PG : store chunks + vectors

== Step 3 — Ask ==
User -> UI : "Who validated 7.1.12.3?"
UI -> RAG : ask (SSE)
RAG -> Cohere : embed question
RAG -> PG : vector + keyword search
PG --> RAG : **top-k chunks**
RAG -> Claude : excerpts + question
Claude --> RAG : answer tokens
RAG --> UI : SSE stream
UI --> User : 💬 answer with [n] citations

note across
  Claude never touches the database: retrieval (vector + BM25, fused)
  happens in rag.py, and Claude only sees the top-k excerpts.
  Full sequence: system-workflow.png
end note

@enduml
